<LegalDocument
  title="Accessibility"
  updated="October 31, 2026"
  description="What Impact Recap does to keep this website usable, which third-party pieces we do not control, and how to tell us about a barrier you run into."
>
  <p>
    Impact Recap wants people to be able to read a sermon recap, browse the
    library, and use the contact form. This statement covers <a href="https://impact-recap.com/">https://impact-recap.com</a>. It describes
    our aim and the limits we already know about. It is not an audit, and it does
    not claim a conformance level.
  </p>
  <p>
    Impact Recap is an independent website, not a public-sector body. This
    statement is not a claim that public-sector accessibility regulations apply.
  </p>

  <h2>How we build pages</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each page has one main heading, and sections follow in order.</li>
    <li>Form fields have labels, and the contact form can be submitted without a script.</li>
    <li>Images that carry meaning have text alternatives. Decorative marks do not.</li>
    <li>Menus, carousels, and the contact form are meant to work from a keyboard.</li>
    <li>A skip link moves past the header to the content.</li>
    <li>When a browser asks for less motion, carousels and transitions stay still.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do not control</h2>
  <p>
    Some pieces come from other services. We do not control their accessibility:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The YouTube player on a sermon page.</li>
    <li>The Google reCAPTCHA checkbox on the contact form, which appears on the published site.</li>
    <li>Fonts and stylesheets loaded from Google Fonts, a Bootstrap CDN, and cdnjs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If something gets in the way, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
    Tell us the page address, what you were trying to do, and what happened. We
    will look into it and reply. We do not publish a separate accessibility phone
    line or email address.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    This statement was prepared on October 31, 2026. If the site changes in a way
    that affects access, we will update this page and the date above.
  </p>
</LegalDocument>
